A||||3||84_duke||Aftermarket wheels.... mm alignment??||||5||
Z||000000||84_duke||11-04-2001||11:58 PM||||I am looking into putting some 17" wheels on my 84, and noticed there are different offsets or alignments measured in mm.  What exactly does this measure?  What is the stock number for this, and just how far can I vary from it?<BR>Thanks <P>------------------<BR>84_duke||||reg||5
Z||000001||Turbo88||11-05-2001||11:05 AM||||The offset is the distance between the inner edge of the rim and the center hub. More offset means the rim/tire will stick farther into your wheel well. Less means the rim/tire will stick farther outside the fender well. To much and you will have rubbing problems. Too little and you look silly <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">..||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||11-05-2001||12:18 PM||||Welllll, Sorta.<P>The offset is actually measured from the <I>centerline of the wheel</I>, to the back of the hub flange. Other than that, your statement is entirely correct.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||11-05-2001||12:20 PM||||I believe it should be about 40 mm (remember a mm isn't very much)<P>Gary||||reg||1
